course: dictionary
lesson: 12338
title: Covert: secret or hidden
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Covert is a word with two meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. As an adjective, it means secret or hidden, done so that people do not notice. «The spies carried out a covert operation at night.» Spies work in secret, so covert must mean hidden.
explain: As a noun, a covert is a thick bush or small wood where wild animals hide. «The fox waited in the covert until the hens came out.» You can picture a fox hiding in the bushes, so here covert is the hiding place.
explain: The opposite of covert is overt, which means done openly, where everyone can see. Check your meaning by putting «secret» or «hidden» into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Covert means secret or hidden, done so that people do not notice.
fact: «Covert operation» means a secret mission, such as one carried out by spies.
fact: A covert is also a thick bush or small wood where wild animals hide.
fact: «Covert» and «overt» are opposites: overt means done openly.
exercise: «The agents carried out a covert operation at night.» What does covert mean here? | *Secret and hidden | Very cold and wet | Loud and open for everyone to see | Written in large letters
exercise: «The fox waited in the covert until the hens came out.» What is a covert in this sentence? | *A thick bush or small wood where animals hide | A big farm building | A loud noise | A type of bird
exercise: Find the opposite of covert. | Secret | Sneaky | Hidden | *Overt
test: «She took a covert glance at the cake before anyone could see.» What does covert mean? | Happy and loud | Out in the open for all to see | Very big and noisy | *Secret, done so no one notices
test: «The deer lay still in the covert, out of sight.» What is a covert here? | *A thick bush or small wood where animals hide | A type of cake | A secret plan | A loud shout
exam: A covert plan is one that is | Done only in the summer | *Done in secret, so people do not notice | Done by a very large crowd | Done in front of everybody
